resman_user_cpu_limit_active{uid, username} \- User limit status (1=limited, 0=unlimited)
.IP \(bu
resman_cpu_points_parent_usage_microseconds_delta \- Effective parent CPU time delivered during the common control-cycle interval; the allocation denominator
.IP \(bu
resman_cpu_points_programmed_sibling_weight_sum and resman_cpu_points_observed_sibling_weight_sum \- Flat scheduling denominator weights
.IP \(bu
resman_cpu_points_parent_throttled_periods_delta and resman_cpu_points_parent_throttled_microseconds_delta \- CFS throttling in the common interval; positive values can be expected under saturation
.IP \(bu
resman_config_reload_state{state} \- One-hot terminal reload state: never, applied, refused, or failed; refused means the disk candidate is pending while the prior epoch remains active
.IP \(bu
resman_config_reload_last_attempt_timestamp_seconds and resman_config_reload_last_success_timestamp_seconds \- Timestamps that distinguish the latest terminal attempt from the latest acknowledged epoch
.IP \(bu
resman_user_cpu_points_configured_guarantee{uid, username} \- Optional mapped-user guarantee; absent for best-effort users
.IP \(bu
resman_user_cpu_points_applied_weight{uid, username} \- Raw verified leaf cpu.weight, not delivered CPU Points
.IP \(bu
resman_user_cpu_points_process_coverage{uid, username, coverage} \- none, complete, partial, or unavailable host-process coverage
.IP \(bu
resman_user_ram_cgroup_memory_current_bytes{uid, username} \- Native slice charges; interpret with typed coverage, not as complete process-derived UID memory
.PP
All per-user series are published exclusively from the authoritative control-cycle
sample. Observation-only refreshes update system-wide telemetry but do not write or
remove per-user series, so CPU alerts and the exported EMA use the same sampling
stream as enforcement.
CPU Points usage and throttling deltas share one explicit interval. Compare sibling or
leaf delivery with effective parent usage, never with the nominal pool or programmed
quota. CFS can under-deliver nominal quota. Unused capacity is available to all runnable user-slice siblings.
